[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"198","stub":{"id":"198","section":"4) Poe Dam to Poe Powerhouse","altname":"Poe Run","river":"Feather, N. Fork","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"442","dateTime":"2026-05-11T23:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Put in at Sandy Beach just downstream of the Poe Dam on river left.","id":"111291","location":{"latitude":"39.803847","longitude":"-121.441131"},"name":"Poe Dam Put-In","distance":"0","photoID":"890350","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"After several class IV rapids a class V+ rapid that was dubbed Four Doors during the flow study.   While this rapid is potentially runnable, no one during the flow study ran this rapid in its entirety.    The current feeds directly into an ugly sieve piton spot which is followed by a bigger sieve.\n\nBoaters can portage on either right or left.  The right side portage is reported to require some technical rock climbing.   The portage on the left is reported to be an easy walk with a 15 foot rappel at the end.\n\nThe video below shows Darin McQuid running this rapid in fall of 2009 around 500 to 600 cfs.   The move from left to right to avoid the sieves looks dangerous\n\n[Four Doors on the Poe Run of the North Fork Feather](http://vimeo.com/7604836) from [Daniel Brasuell](http://vimeo.com/user563218) on [Vimeo](http://vimeo.com).","id":"100300","location":{"latitude":"39.78860092163086","longitude":"-121.4489974975586"},"name":"Four Doors","distance":"1.4","photoID":"614747","difficulty":"VI","approximate":true},{"type":"waterfall","description":"This 12 to 15 foot drop is difficult to run and stay upright.  It is named after Gordon Patchin whose run of a big rapid is described in the Holbeck and Stanley book.  However, that write up suggests that this rapid was actually portaged and Gordon lead the charge on the rapid immediately upstream.  Hard to know.","id":"100299","location":{"latitude":"39.775701","longitude":"-121.452004"},"name":"Patchin's Passion","distance":"2.41","difficulty":"V","approximate":true,"photoID":"zurjrjvXs5c6Yv5mNwNKF"},{"type":"put-in","description":"This access point allows boaters the option of only boating the more difficult upper section or the easier lower section. A road bridge crosses the river here making it easy to find.","id":"100229","location":{"latitude":"39.769589","longitude":"-121.457804"},"name":"Bardees Bar","distance":"2.98","photoID":"639818","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":true},{"type":"rapid","description":"The last major rapid on the run, and one of the most significant. Scout on river left by taking out on the bar above the rapid or catching an eddy on the left before entering the main part of the rapid.","id":"TIMrD3Im1FjS6pKGEeB5G","location":{"latitude":"39.72854667","longitude":"-121.46724764"},"name":"Bridge View","distance":"6.62","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"RSv3u455AnfW7SwSUpRWO"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Good access on river left at the Poe Powerhouse.","id":"116559","location":{"latitude":"39.721916","longitude":"-121.469883"},"name":"Poe Powerhouse Take-Out","distance":"7.25","photoID":"wjSnhbYupN57xVyLhD1Pw","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"IlXCGswszSVy7pAeOEEEN","title":"Jan 2025 Bardees Rd Washout and Repair Schedule","post_date":"2025-01-28 18:52:59+00","detail":"As of 1/27/2025, PG&E was aware of some severe washouts to Bardee's Bar Road with plans to repair them \"this week.\" Anticipate some access impacts at Bardee's Bar Road through early February.","user":{"name":"Thomas O'Keefe"}},{"id":"BRvon3XfXMTKx4cKyNQc0","title":"River Page \"Next Release\" Inaccurate as of 9/26/24 ","post_date":"2024-09-26 23:28:43+00","detail":"There will be releases on Poe 9/28 + 9/29. The River Page's \"Next Release\" box appears to be loading the 10/12 + 10/13 weekend releases instead. Flows will be 1400cfs from 9am-3pm on both weekends!","user":{"name":"Jeff Venturino"}}],"photos":[{"id":"3KwRb1NKMB1TIUTHNoj81","ext":"jpg","post_id":"RFpGEeHflwx99yQHNvZ72","description":"Rapic is still full at this flow","caption":"Tinky Winky Low Flow","poi_name":null,"subject":"Martin Roland / Chris Hest","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":"100613","photo_date":"2019-08-04T05:06:54.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:06:55.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3KwRb1NKMB1TIUTHNoj81","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3KwRb1NKMB1TIUTHNoj81"}},{"id":"Z98j4nSr2VGN5VmCdEvFU","ext":"jpg","post_id":"RFpGEeHflwx99yQHNvZ72","description":"Good view of the peace sign rock to the right of Hest","caption":"Peace Out","poi_name":null,"subject":"Chris Hest","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":"107308","photo_date":"2019-08-04T05:06:54.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:06:55.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Z98j4nSr2VGN5VmCdEvFU","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Z98j4nSr2VGN5VmCdEvFU"}},{"id":"rdT9wnMqxWlEf8qPKPeWJ","ext":"jpg","post_id":"RFpGEeHflwx99yQHNvZ72","description":"","caption":" Hest in Dipsy","poi_name":null,"subject":"Chris Hest","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2019-08-04T05:06:55.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:06:55.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/rdT9wnMqxWlEf8qPKPeWJ","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/rdT9wnMqxWlEf8qPKPeWJ"}},{"id":"RSv3u455AnfW7SwSUpRWO","ext":"jpg","post_id":"RFpGEeHflwx99yQHNvZ72","description":"Last major rapid on the run","caption":"Bridge View","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2019-08-04T05:06:55.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:06:55.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/RSv3u455AnfW7SwSUpRWO","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/RSv3u455AnfW7SwSUpRWO"}},{"id":"TdJbxmZRVn2QHrWWaDiXF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"RFpGEeHflwx99yQHNvZ72","description":"More rocks for sure but still very runnable.","caption":"Tinky Winky Scout ","poi_name":null,"subject":"Chris Hest","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":"100613","photo_date":"2019-08-04T05:06:55.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:06:55.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/TdJbxmZRVn2QHrWWaDiXF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/TdJbxmZRVn2QHrWWaDiXF"}},{"id":"14747","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8740","description":"<p>This is the begining of the Poe Canyon run.</p>","caption":"Poe Canyon","poi_name":"Pulga Bridge","subject":"Roland McNutt","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":"100303","photo_date":"2004-04-17T05:19:10.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:19:11.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14747","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14747"}},{"id":"zurjrjvXs5c6Yv5mNwNKF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"8740","description":"15 foot drop with a big hit at the bottom.","caption":"Patchin's Passion","poi_name":null,"subject":"Dave Steindorf","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":"100299","photo_date":"2004-04-17T05:19:10.000Z","updated_at":"2025-11-19T05:19:11.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/zurjrjvXs5c6Yv5mNwNKF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/zurjrjvXs5c6Yv5mNwNKF"}},{"id":"16528","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8739","description":"","caption":"Upper Poe","poi_name":"The Slot","subject":"Charlie Guilbault","author":"Dave Steindorf","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16528","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16528"}},{"id":"890350","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892705","description